    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** leading our projections at a 70.30 efficiency score; he is our premier target to secure the scarcest category, stolen bases, as he faces a favorable matchup against Abbott. Similarly, **Casey Schmitt** (63.20) benefits from a juicy matchup against Lorenzen, with his dynamic platoon edge boosting his value well above his base projection. We are also leaning heavily into **Yordan Alvarez** (61.80) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (60.59), who despite some platoon constraints and pending lineups, offer elite xwOBA profiles and soft matchups that keep them comfortably above our threshold for elite output.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's roster was keeping **Carson Benge** (40.59) on the bench. He sat right on the edge of our efficiency floor, but ultimately lost out to the higher-floor projections of **Colt Keith** and **Caleb Durbin**. Meanwhile, we avoided the sub-40 danger zone with **Gary Sanchez**, **Lars Nootbaar**, and **Dillon Dingler**, all of whom were benched to preserve game caps against elite arms like Skenes and Wheeler. Note that while **Trea Turner**, **Kyle Schwarber**, and **Christian Yelich** remain locked into the starting lineup, their scores are suppressed today by the presence of Skubal and Skenes; proceed with caution as these elite arms pose a legitimate risk to our batting average categories.",
